"1579","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1579 Arabic Hadees: 1257"
"1580","On the authority of ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), attributed to the Prophet (ﷺ): ""O ʿĀʾishah! Were it not that your people are recent converts from polytheism (and I do not have sufficient means to rebuild it), I would have spent the treasure of the Kaʿbah in the cause of Allah, and I would have demolished the Kaʿbah and leveled it to the ground, then rebuilt it upon the foundations of Ibrāhīm, and I would have made for it two doors set at ground level—an eastern door through which people would enter, and a western door through which they would exit—and I would have added six cubits to it from the Ḥijr."" In a narration: ""And I would have included the Ḥijr within it, for Quraysh had shortened it when they built the Kaʿbah. If your people should decide to rebuild it after me, come, let me show you what they left out of it."" So he showed her approximately seven cubits.

In a narration from her: She said, ""I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the Jidar (the wall)—meaning the Ḥijr—'Is it part of the House?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'Then why did they not include it in the House?' He said: 'Your people ran short of funds.' I said: 'What is the matter with its door being raised high?' He said: 'Your people did that so they could admit whom they wished and prevent whom they wished.'""

In a narration: ""...out of arrogance, so that none would enter it except whom they wished. Thus, when a man wished to enter it, they would let him climb up until, when he was about to enter, they would push him, so he would fall. Were it not that your people are recent converts from the Jāhiliyyah, and I fear their hearts would deny [the change], I would have included the Jidar in the House and set its door at ground level.""

(So when Ibn al-Zubayr gained authority, he demolished it and made for it two doors.) In a narration: ""That is what prompted Ibn al-Zubayr to demolish it."" Yazīd ibn Rūmān said: ""I witnessed Ibn al-Zubayr when he demolished it and rebuilt it, and he included the Ḥijr within it. I saw the foundations of Ibrāhīm (peace be upon him); they were stones interlocked like the humps of camels, tightly interlocked."""
